{
  "_": "The three-hit normal-attack combo, per weapon type and per character build. `length` is the animation's own frame count; `chain_opens`/`chain_closes` are the frames between which a follow-up press continues the combo. Regenerate with tools/plyevents.py.",
  "_source": "player/NN_<weapon>_<build>_pa00.narc each carry one DSIF whose region A is 22 fixed 152-byte records, one per animation in file order. The two window frames are bytes +0x04 and +0x05 of the record; 0xFF means none.",
  "_validation": "Frame-exact emulator traces agree on TEN boundaries across two weapons: rifle atk1 chains at 16 and 32 and not at 12 or 36 (table 16..32); rifle atk2 chains at 20, 24, 28 and not 16 or 32 (17..31); handgun atk1 chains at 16 and 24 and not 12 or 28 (15..24).",
  "_units": "FRAMES of the attack animation at playback rate 1.0. The rate lives at 0x021A2184 (0x1000 = 1.0); a state running the 'Even Quicker Anims' cheat at 0x2000 halves every observed number.",
  "_atk3": "atk3 never carries a window -- there is no fourth hit to chain into. grenade(12) and l_cannon(13) have only atk1 and no combo at all.",
  "_anomaly": "16_slicer is the only weapon whose windows close at or AFTER its animation ends -- atk1 20..39 against a 33-frame animation, atk2 10..59 against 35. Not measured, not explained, and left in rather than trimmed: it is either a property of a thrown weapon or a sign the reading is incomplete for this type.",
  "_not_established": "which weapon types each CLASS may equip. This table is a superset; class restrictions have not been read out of the game.",
