  "_hits": "hit_frames are the frames damage lands, read from bytes +0x08..+0x0C of the same record -- ascending, 0xFF-terminated, one entry per damage instance. Five weapon types strike more than once with a normal attack: unarmed, dagger, claw, double saber and machinegun. The Japanese wiki independently names the multi-hit weapons as dual daggers, claws, dual swords and machine guns -- the same set, its only omission being unarmed, which has no weapon page.",
  "_not_identified": "The SOUND cue is not among the fields identified here, and it was not measurable either: melonDS's GDB stub returns zeros for I/O space, so the SPU channel registers cannot be sampled per frame. Byte +0x10 is NOT a frame -- it takes six values across 252 records (5, 6, 11, 12, 17, 18) and tracks the weapon's heft rather than its timing -- so an earlier description of it as frame-sized is withdrawn. +0x01 is 3 in every record and carries nothing per-animation."
}
